BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Morehead Planetarium & Science Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T190000
DTSTAMP:20260803T000434
CREATED:20260701T161607Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260709T140913Z
UID:39835-1785866400-1785870000@moreheadplanetarium.org
SUMMARY:Carolina Science Cafe: GLP-1s
DESCRIPTION:What are GLP-1s?\n\n\n\nSee you at August’s Carolina Science Cafe! In this session\, Dr. Jonathan Campbell of Duke University will present a brief history of the evolution of GLP-1 medications and where this field is heading. \n\n\n\nDesigned for adults\, Carolina Science Cafe is a free program that explores science topics making national and international headlines\, offering the chance to meet the experts behind the work. This special program is hosted at Haw River Tap & Table in Carrboro on the first Tuesday of every month. Light appetizers are available for all attendees. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout the Speaker\n\n\n\nDr. Jonathan Campbell is an associate professor of medicine at Duke University and a member of the Duke Molecular Physiology Institute. His group studies how incretins like GLP-1 work to regulate metabolism in the context of health\, diabetes\, obesity\, and related diseases.  \n\n\n\n\nMore about Dr. Campbell’s work\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCarolina Science Cafe is produced by Morehead Planetarium and Science Center and sponsored by the UNC Chapter of Sigma Xi. \n\n\n\nYou do not need to register…just show up!
URL:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/carolina-science-cafe-glp1/
LOCATION:Haw River Tap & Table\, 300 E Main St C\, Carrboro\, NC\, 27510\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs,Teen And Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Carolina-Science-Cafe-1920x842-1.jpeg
END:VEVENT
